cff-version: 1.2.0
title: STRATA-NOVA
message: >-
  If you use STRATA-NOVA, please cite this software version and the upstream
  SNEC and SuperSNEC works. For DDT/HESMA inputs and references, cite the
  archive and model/product papers listed below. For W7, cite Nomoto et al.
  (1984) and Thielemann et al. (1986); Moriya et al. (2023) describes the
  wind-comparison setup. For SN 2017cbv observations, cite Wee et al. (2018),
  CDS/VizieR J/ApJ/863/90 and the VizieR service. Archive acknowledgement
  wording is provided in THIRD_PARTY.md and Analysis/DATA/README.md.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - given-names: Alexandru
    family-names: Tudorache
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
keywords:
  - Type Ia supernovae
  - circumstellar material
  - radiation hydrodynamics
  - SNEC
  - light curves
abstract: >-
  STRATA-NOVA is a one-dimensional Lagrangian grey radiation-hydrodynamics
  extension of SuperSNEC/SNEC for Type Ia supernovae and circumstellar
  interaction. It includes attached r^-2/r^-3 CSM envelopes, a Badenes
  accretion-wind prescription, finite constant-density shells, a native
  staged sequential-encounter manager, Type Ia profile handling, observer
  light-travel approximations, and radioactive-heating optimizations inherited
  from SuperSNEC.
